sentences.l:
and around it I poured a libation to all the dead,
first with honey-mixture, and after that with sweet wine,
the third time again with water;

And them, when with vows and prayers, the tribes of the dead,
I had entreated, the sheep taking, I cut their throats
into the pit, and flowed the blood, dark-clouded;

In Circe’s hall, lying down, I did not think
to go back down, going to the long ladder,
but straight down from the roof I fell;

And now you I entreat by those behind, who are not present,
by your wife and father, who reared you when you were small,
and Telemachus, whom alone in your halls you left;

We two thus, with words exchanging, hateful,
sat, I on one side over the blood the sword holding,
and the phantom on the other side of my companion much was speaking;

